{{right|''R. N. Cust'', Mod. Lang. E. Indies, p. 62.}}}}
'''6.''' From the proper destination or purpose: as, to keep ''back'' despatches.
{{smaller block|A certain man named Ananias, with Sapphira his wife, sold a possession, and kept ''back'' part of the price.
{{right|Acts v. 1, 2.}}}}
'''7.''' Away from an undertaking, engagement, or promise.
{{smaller block|<poem>I’ve been surprised in an unguarded hour,
But must not now go ''back''.</poem>
{{right|''Addison.''}}}}

